'''Akio Yabe''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that was added in [[Version 6.8 Update|Version 6.8]] and is exclusive to the [[Power Pro Baseball Collaboration Event]]. He is acquired after beating any [[Power Pro Baseball Collaboration Event#Sophomore Summer|Sophomore Summer]] stages. His [[True Form]] was given in the same update and gains Area Attack, the ability to perform [[Wave Attack]]s and increased health and range, but loses multi-hit and halves damage.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 385
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Akio Yabe
|name2 = Akio Yabe CC
|name3 = Akio & Gunder CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Akio Yabe CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Akio & Gunder CC''' when obtained from [[Willing Sacrifice (Deadly)|Willing Sacrifice]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Akio Yabe is essentially useless in all but a few early stages due to rather low stats and Single Target.

==='''True Form'''===
Akio & Gunder CC can be used as a peon clearer for weaker peons (e.g. [[Doge]], [[Croco]], [[Squire Rel]], etc.) although [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]] in all forms is better for this. They can be used in 4-crown stages as a replacement for Crazed Gross, although their wave is shorter and later-game wavers such as [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] outclass them completely.

